# Nightscout Cockpit - Project Rails

## A. Security and Privacy
- Nightscout token never sent to the client; server-side only.
- Tokens encrypted-at-rest (Fernet via APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY); never logged (including query strings).
- CORS strict: only CORS_ORIGINS frontend origin.
- Auth required for all /me/* endpoints.
- Rate limiting on auth and data endpoints (in-memory for MVP).
- HTTPS assumed in production; local HTTP ok.

## B. Code Quality
- Pydantic models for API responses.
- Separate modules: fetch - parsing - metrics - aggregation.
- Type hints on all functions.
- Basic tests for aggregation/processing modules.
- No hardcoded localhost in containers: frontend uses BACKEND_URL env (docker: http://backend:8000).

## C. UX
- No placeholder text about endpoint not available in production UI.
- Clear empty-states: Geen data in dit venster.
- Units toggle mg/dL vs mmol/L (convert for display only; internal = mg/dL).
- Live dashboard uses time.sleep() + do_rerun() compat helper; no meta-refresh.
- Show Last update, Data age, Coverage percent clearly.

## D. Performance
- Cache live endpoint TTL 15-30s.
- Cache insights endpoint TTL 300s.
- Nightscout fetch counts large enough for window/range (14d = 25000 entries).
- Resample to 5-min grid for aggregations.

## E. Nightscout Data Sources (AAPS)
- CGM: GET /api/v1/entries/sgv.json?count=N&token=T
- Temp Basal: GET /api/v1/treatments.json?count=N&token=T with eventType Temp Basal
